  "descriptions": [
    {
      "source": "DeFiHackLabs",
      "text": "Sandwich attack. Lost: 81.68 ETH"
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "On January 25, 2021, Badger DAO's DIGG,WBTC pool on SushiSwap was exploited via a swap-path misconfiguration in SushiMaker. The attacker created an illiquid DIGG,WETH pair, drained accumulated DIGG rewards for 81 ETH, and swapped them at favorable rates. This affected XSUSHI fee earnings but not user vaults. SushiMaker relied on default swap bridges, with no custom bridge set for DIGG. DIGG fees accumulated and, when converted, were swapped through a user-created, illiquid DIGG,WETH pool. The absence of a bridge allowed outsized rewards to the attacker."
    }
  ],
